{
 "title": "No value: Optional",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "In safe Greengold code **there is no `null`**. If a function sometimes cannot return a value, its return type is `Optional[T]`. It has two states: `Valid(value)` (there is a value) and `None` (there is not). With `match` you must handle both."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "fn find_index(items: []i32, target: i32) -> Optional[usize]:",
    "    for idx, val in items:",
    "        if val == target:",
    "            return Valid(idx)",
    "    return None",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    numbers: [4]i32 = [10, 25, 40, 85]",
    "    match find_index(numbers, 40):",
    "        Valid(idx):",
    "            print(\"found at\", idx)",
    "        None:",
    "            print(\"not in the array\")",
    "    match find_index(numbers, 7):",
    "        Valid(idx):",
    "            print(\"found at\", idx)",
    "        None:",
    "            print(\"not in the array\")"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "found at 2",
    "not in the array"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c08-l01-x1",
   "prompt": "Write `first_negative(items: []i32) -> Optional[i32]`: the first negative number as `Valid`, or `None` if there is none. For `[3, 8, -2, 5]` print the result with `match`.",
   "starter": [
    "fn first_negative(items: []i32) -> Optional[i32]:",
    "    return None",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    data: [4]i32 = [3, 8, -2, 5]",
    "    match first_negative(data):",
    "        Valid(x):",
    "            print(\"found\", x)",
    "        None:",
    "            print(\"none\")"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "fn first_negative(items: []i32) -> Optional[i32]:",
    "    for x in items:",
    "        if x < 0:",
    "            return Valid(x)",
    "    return None",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    data: [4]i32 = [3, 8, -2, 5]",
    "    match first_negative(data):",
    "        Valid(x):",
    "            print(\"found\", x)",
    "        None:",
    "            print(\"none\")"
   ],
   "hint": "In the loop, `return Valid(x)` when `x < 0`.",
   "expected": [
    "found -2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c08-l01-q1",
   "q": "Which two states does `Optional[T]` have?",
   "options": [
    "`Ok` and `Err`",
    "`Valid` and `None`",
    "`True` and `False`"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "`Ok`/`Err` belong to `Result`."
  }
 ]
}
